Compost-Template version 0.06
=============================

Compost::Template is a perl templating module, originally based on
HTML::Template, and like HTML::Template attempts to make using
templates simple and natural.

Compost::Template has a more elegant syntax that solves the problems
i had with HTML::Template.  It also compiles the Template into a
simple bytecode format, that is fast to interpret.

Compost::Template is useful for web templating, but also for other
templating jobs, it's features include...

 * cleaner syntax
 * better whitespce control
 * printf, to manage padding  
 * more flexible than HTML::Template
 * a state namespace, that is globable
 * able to manage callbacks
 * template errors contain line numbers

For more information, perldoc Compost::Template

Compost::Template was part of my Compost cms, which is still being
developed and pondered.  Compost cms is a simple lightweight cms,
a mix of old-skool perl cgi with modern web framework ideas.
It is not a web programming framework, end users are not expected
to be able to program.

INSTALLATION

To install this module type the following:

   perl Makefile.PL
   make
   make test
   make install

DEPENDENCIES

This module requires these other modules and libraries:

File::Spec
Test::More - but only for testing the build

PROBLEMS/BUG REPORTS

Please send any reports of problems or bugs to banjo@actrix.co.nz.

If you know Test::More, and can be bothered making a Test case,
email it to me, that'll help me find and fix the bug.

If you'd like more features, or have suggestions or whatever,
please email me.

